## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to combine learned features with classical cues under tight on-device latency, in a realistic retail robotics setting.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight CNN + classical feature fusion
- On-device few-shot adaptation (3-5 shots)
- Latency budgeting (<=50 ms/frame)
- Robust evaluation: per-item accuracy, misorientation metrics, throughput

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch of forward pass
function forward(frame) {
  const rois = detectROIs(frame);
  for (const roi of rois) {
    const cnnFeat = smallCNN(roi);
    const cues = extractCues(roi); // hist, edges, texture
    const fused = fuse(cnnFeat, cues);
    const label = orientationHead(fused);
    if (label === 'misoriented') alert(roi);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle label drift with new item designs?
- What ablation studies would you run to verify cue contributions?

